## Tin
component-tin = Tin
    .genitive = tin
component-tin-description-novice = A soft silvery metal. It melts at just 232 °C — even a spirit lamp can melt it. Tin is used to solder wires.
component-tin-description-school = Tin melts at 231.9 °C; its latent heat of fusion is ≈ 59 kJ/kg. While it melts its temperature stays the same — the heating graph shows a flat “shelf”.
component-tin-safety-school = Molten tin is very hot (over 230 °C) and causes bad burns. Water in the melt boils at once and spatters the metal.
